bgfx presents a caller-provided EGL context's current surface itself (GlContext::swap), although the host that
provided the context presents it (src/libs/ui/android/jni_host.cpp under a GLSurfaceView, which swaps after
onDrawFrame): every frame showed a second, undrawn buffer, black or a frame older, seen as the launcher's buttons
flashing between pressed, black and normal on a tap. With a caller-provided context bgfx does not swap.

diff --git a/src/glcontext_egl.cpp b/src/glcontext_egl.cpp
